## 5. Before-and-after addenda (`What happened after the switch-over`)

- **The DevPass GLM route.** The fan-out could reach GLM-5.3-Flash only through per-token routes while the operator held a flat-price DevPass plan; `041-cli-pi-devpass-glm-route` moved the bare `glm-5.3-flash` literal to `llmgateway` and gave `cli-pi` the two credential prefixes Pi's own config declares (spec.md:41,60,76). GLM-5.3-Flash through opencode-go is now direct-dispatch only (implementation-summary.md:59).
- **The test debt under the suite.** `042-deep-loop-test-debt` fixed the deep-loop-owned red tests in the spec-kit CLI suite at the producer — the council persistence guard's first-write case — and aligned three stale assertions to contracts later commits had superseded, rather than reversing those decisions to make tests pass (spec.md:36-38; implementation-summary.md:59,63-65). The deep-loop runtime typecheck went from 53 errors to zero (implementation-summary.md:112).
- **The review leaf's two duties.** `043-review-leaf-protocol` wrote the verbatim-path duty and the max-iterations stop-reason duty into the lineage prompt and the deep-review agent contract, so the leaf is told what the runner already enforces (spec.md:46; implementation-summary.md:52). It also repointed three determinism tests at the runtime's own vitest binary, 132 of 132 green (implementation-summary.md:94).
- **The second DevPass route.** `044-cli-pi-devpass-deepseek-route` applied the GLM fix to DeepSeek V4 Flash after opencode-go's monthly window closed and rejected every lane, moving the bare `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` literal to `llmgateway` (spec.md:38,53). The second research round could then run at `max` on the flat-price plan (spec.md:98).
- **Containment that preserves.** `045-fanout-write-containment-hardening` turned the containment remedy from irreversible revert to quarantine-and-preserve after the guard reverted 1,858 paths of a concurrent session and failed a completed lane (spec.md:22,39,68). Restore, when opted into, now targets pre-dispatch bytes, outcome separation keeps a finished lane fulfilled, and the worktree isolation phase was later removed once attribution was ruled out of scope (spec.md:24,42; implementation-summary.md:101).

Composition reminder: the section's intro sentence names "the children that follow, numbered 013 through 028" and the 2026-09-05 merge (`before-and-after.md:188`); it needs a parallel mention of the five 2026-09-20 merged packets.

