## 7. Contradictions / exceptions

**041 — status contest (spec.md vs graph-metadata vs tasks).**
`spec.md:26` and `implementation-summary.md:17,42` declare Complete; `graph-metadata.json:42` says `"status": "in_progress"`; `tasks.md:66-67,79-80` retain T014 (whole runtime suite not run) and T017 (end-to-end iteration not proven) as NOT DONE. The implementation summary states both limitations itself (`implementation-summary.md:112`, and the T014 follow-up at `:114`). Completion of the routing fix is verified (`implementation-summary.md:95`); completion of the two verification tasks is not. Proposed row keeps `complete`/`confirmed`; downgrade to `in_progress` if open tasks are binding.

**042 — no contradictions.** `spec.md:26`, `implementation-summary.md:46`, `graph-metadata.json:42` all Complete; no `acceptance-criteria.md`; no unchecked tasks. Exceptions are recorded limitations only: the full CLI project is 1568/1589 with the single red file attributed to the in-flight 036 packet (`implementation-summary.md:110`), and the runtime suite carries 9 pre-existing red files described as environment-dependent or contract-drift (`implementation-summary.md:113`).

**043 — no contradictions.** `spec.md:25`, `implementation-summary.md:43`, `graph-metadata.json:40` all Complete; no `acceptance-criteria.md`; no unchecked tasks. Exception: the whole runtime suite hung and was not run (`implementation-summary.md:105`).

**044 — no contradictions.** `spec.md:25`, `implementation-summary.md:43`, `graph-metadata.json:42` all Complete; no `acceptance-criteria.md`; no unchecked tasks. Exceptions: the route was proven at `low`, not `max` (`implementation-summary.md:103`); and the round-two note says the first launch still reached opencode-go because worktree 046 ran its own copy of the driver (`implementation-summary.md:94`) — a reference to a worktree mechanism that packet 045's phase 007 later removed (`045.../spec.md:42`), so that sentence is dated.

**045 — four contradictions, all about the removed checkout watch and stale metadata; the closure decision itself is consistent.**
1. **AC-018 vs the delivered tree.** `acceptance-criteria.md:80` marks AC-018 (`checkout_write_detected` / `checkout_watched` reporting) as `Met`, and `acceptance-criteria.md:107` says "the checkout-watch extension rows await the same sign-off"; `implementation-summary.md:110` records the watch GREEN and `implementation-summary.md:17` lists its sign-off as the `next_safe_action`. Against that, `spec.md:42` says the checkout watch "was removed in phase 007 under ADR-007", and `decision-record.md:470` marks ADR-005 "Superseded by ADR-007; the watch left with the mechanism it guarded". Ground truth from the tree: `checkout_write_detected`/`checkout_watched` have zero references anywhere under `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/`, and `tests/unit/worktree-lifecycle.vitest.ts` no longer exists (only `tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/worktree-fixture.ts` remains). AC-018 should be `Superseded`/named to ADR-007, or the reversal note and ADR-005 status should be corrected — one of the two document sets is wrong.
2. **Closure count.** `acceptance-criteria.md:107` says "the two worktree rows are superseded by ADR-007" while the table has three Superseded rows — AC-009 `:71`, AC-015 `:77`, AC-017 `:79` — and the closure lead at `:105` says "the three worktree rows".
3. **Mixed "final state" evidence.** `implementation-summary.md:110` reports "full suite from the final state: 156 files passed, 2654 passed", but the phase-007 row reports "151 files / 2568 tests after the worktree removal in 007"; the watch row's "final state" predates the removal and is not the current tree.
4. **graph-metadata children staleness.** `graph-metadata.json:7-18` mixes planning-phase child names that no longer exist (`001-skip-worktree-cone` :7, `004-eighth-dependency-root` :10, `006-shared-root-write-escape` :12, `007-reducer-ordered-lists` :13, `008-reclaim-relocated-trees` :14) with the executed child set, duplicating suffixes (`006-reducer-ordered-lists` :17 alongside :13; `002-iteration-record-dedupe` and `005-churn-cumulative-arm` appear in both groups), against the current 20-child table at `045.../spec.md:110-131`. Regenerate before committing if graph metadata ships.

**Cross-cutting exception.** Only 045 has an `acceptance-criteria.md`; 041–044 are Level 1 and their completion rests on `spec.md` status rows plus implementation-summary verification tables. Where a claim rests only on a declared status and not on an observed check, this draft says so (041).

